WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.450
this is a great story to not only communicate
to you things going on in the real world,

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:09.640
but also to talk about how narratives are
created and framed by corporate media.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.240
So listen, basically support for impeaching.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:19.441
Donald Trump went up when a news of the Ukraine
fiasco first broke hitting about 46 47% and

00:00:19.441 --> 00:00:23.510
then throughout everything that we've seen
happen publicly related to Ukraine and Trump,

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:30.770
so far as support for impeachment has crept
up to 50% 52% 55% depending on which poll

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:31.770
look at.

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:34.000
Now, that by itself is big news.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.600
This is a lot more impeachment support than
there was for Richard Nixon early in Watergate.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.699
It's not normal when it comes to previous
presidents.

00:00:42.699 --> 00:00:49.929
Obama, Bush, as much as Obama and Bush were
hated by the right and left respectively.

00:00:49.929 --> 00:00:53.960
You didn't have more than half the country
saying that the president should be impeached

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:55.920
when it was Obama and Bush.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.460
So now we have a new poll.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:02.999
The poll happens to be from Fox news of all
places, and it says, indeed, 54% of the country

00:01:02.999 --> 00:01:05.360
wants Donald Trump impeached.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:10.110
Now, you might notice that I'm leaving out
a piece of information here, and I did it

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:15.020
on purpose for the, uh, for the, for the purposes
of our story today, I did this deliberately.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:18.680
When I say 54% of the country wants Trump
impeached.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:24.420
If you are a media literate individual, if
you're a savvy thinker, you should be saying,

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:32.440
does David mean 54% want Trump impeached by
the house or is David saying 54% want Trump

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:36.120
impeached and removed via a conviction in
the Senate?

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.640
That is the right question to be asking and
that is exactly the game that is being played

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:40.640
with these numbers.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:46.460
The game that's being played in lots of corporate
media is that they aren't specifying clearly

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:53.810
whether by impeachment people understand that
to mean or are meaning to say that they want

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:59.730
the house to impeach and a trial in the Senate
whose outcome could be one thing or the other

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:00.730
thing.

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:05.270
Or are people saying when they say they want
to impeach, we want Trump convicted and removed

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:06.730
by the Senate.

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:10.239
In this poll, 54% want Trump impeached.

00:02:10.239 --> 00:02:14.159
50% want Trump impeached and removed.

00:02:14.159 --> 00:02:19.090
Meaning that there is 4% in there that want
Trump impeached in the house but not necessarily

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.590
removed by the Senate.

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:23.060
So this is already one game that can be played.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:28.260
You can talk about support is up versus support
is down, but by not specifying whether you're

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:32.540
talking about impeachment only or impeachment
and removal, you can kind of pick whichever

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:36.299
result is closer to suiting your view in the
narrative you want to craft.

00:02:36.299 --> 00:02:40.680
This is how you simultaneously had some networks
saying impeachment hearings have destroyed

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.989
support for Trump impeachment and you had
other media outlets saying support for impeachment

00:02:44.989 --> 00:02:45.989
is up.

00:02:45.989 --> 00:02:50.400
Since the hearings have started, if you want
to say support for impeachment is growing,

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:54.950
you choose a poll that shows it, even if it's
just for articles of impeachment and not removal

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:55.950
or vice versa.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:03:01.079
I think that you understand the other game
that is being played is the momentum game

00:03:01.079 --> 00:03:02.670
after hearing started.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:03.670
Right?

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:04.670
Wow.

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:07.860
The hearings have really deflated the impeachment
movement.

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:12.749
And then at the other time you have some saying,
wow, the hearings are really growing support

00:03:12.749 --> 00:03:13.829
for Trump impeachment.

00:03:13.829 --> 00:03:16.319
Now, how could both be true?

00:03:16.319 --> 00:03:17.779
Just look at different polls.

00:03:17.779 --> 00:03:23.049
So the real story is not the two to three
points swings and impeachment support because

00:03:23.049 --> 00:03:24.719
that's all that we're seeing.

00:03:24.719 --> 00:03:28.529
Tons of people don't even know what's going
on or at least aren't paying attention daily.

00:03:28.529 --> 00:03:34.689
So the real story here is roughly half the
country wants Trump impeached and removed

00:03:34.689 --> 00:03:37.099
the numbers going up and down to three points.

00:03:37.099 --> 00:03:38.590
That's really not a big deal.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:44.170
What's not normal is that half the country
wants the president impeached and removed.

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:50.590
But most importantly, if you look at the internals
of the polls, there's a big polling gap in

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:51.919
favor of impeachment.

00:03:51.919 --> 00:03:59.099
If I only tell you 50% wants Trump removed,
you might assume, Oh, so 50% does not want

00:03:59.099 --> 00:04:00.099
from removed.

00:04:00.099 --> 00:04:03.180
It's dead even it's an even split wrong.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:07.420
Lots of people respond that they don't know
or they aren't sure.

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:11.690
So in the Fox news poll, 50% want him impeached
and removed.

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:17.489
4% want him just impeached and 41% say don't
impeach.

00:04:17.489 --> 00:04:23.949
That means it is not 50 50 it is a plus 13
the people that want an impeachment versus

00:04:23.949 --> 00:04:25.270
the people that do not.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:26.639
That's huge.

00:04:26.639 --> 00:04:27.930
That's what really matters.

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:34.479
Do not be tricked by crafty reporting into
taking your eye off of the ball, which is

00:04:34.479 --> 00:04:39.300
that half the country wants Trump removed
and there is a plus 13 gap of people that

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.949
want impeachment over people that do not.

00:04:41.949 --> 00:04:47.330
It won't change whether it happens of course,
but don't fall for the games that the corporate

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:48.341
media is playing around impeachment polls.

